  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace to understand the current state.\nTest runner is `bun test`. Let me confirm the failure first.\nBaseline confirmed failing. Now the minimal fix — `a - b` should be `a + b`:\nFixed and verified.\n\n## The bug\n\n`src/add.ts` returned `a - b` — the subtraction operator where addition was required:\n\n```ts\nexport function add(a: number, b: number) { return a - b }\n```\n\n## The fix\n\nA one-token change, `a - b` → `a + b`:\n\n```ts\nexport function add(a: number, b: number) { return a + b }\n```\n\n## Verification\n\nTest runner is `bun test` (the test imports from `bun:test`), so no config or runner changes were needed — `package.json` has no scripts and I left it alone.\n\n| Stage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Before | `1 fail` — `Expected: 5, Received: -1` on `add(2,3)` |\n| After | `1 pass`, `0 fail`, 5 `expect()` calls, 1 file |\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` are byte-identical to their original SHA-256 hashes; the public signature `(a: number, b: number) => number` is unchanged, so no callers or tests were touched."
